<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">Projects & Teams</h1>
<p class="text-sm font-normal text-[#8A8A93] leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-10">
    Projects are logical containers used to organize your monitors and access control within HealthyCron.
</p>

<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-white mb-4 mt-8">Organizing with Projects</h2>
<p class="text-sm font-normal text-[#8A8A93] leading-relaxed mb-4">
    We recommend grouping your monitors into projects by environment or by service boundaries. For example:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Create a <strong>"Production"</strong> project for critical user-facing jobs. Route these alerts directly to PagerDuty or an on-call phone number.</li>
    <li>Create a <strong>"Staging"</strong> project for testing. Route these alerts to a low-priority Slack channel or ignore them entirely.</li>
</ul>

<p class="text-sm font-normal text-[#8A8A93] leading-relaxed mt-4">
    Monitors can be moved between projects freely from the Dashboard. Each project maintains its own isolated set of Integrations; a monitor in Staging cannot accidentally trigger an Integration assigned exclusively to Production.
</p>

<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-white mb-4 mt-12">Managing Teams</h2>
<p class="text-sm font-normal text-[#8A8A93] leading-relaxed mb-6">
    You can invite team members to collaborate on a Project by navigating to the Project Settings and initiating an email invitation. Roles are scoped <em>per project</em>.
</p>

<div class="docs-table-wrapper mb-12">
    <table class="docs-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Role</th>
                <th>Permissions</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Owner</td>
                <td>Full access. Can create/edit/delete monitors, configure ping settings, add/remove integrations, and invite or remove other members.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Member</td>
                <td>Read/Write access to monitors. They can pause monitors and view logs, but cannot edit integrations or invite new members to the project.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-info mt-12">
    <div class="callout-title">
        <span class="callout-icon">ℹ</span>
        Project Ping Keys
    </div>
    <div class="callout-body">
        Each project generates a specific <strong>Ping Key</strong> for Auto-Provisioning. When a ping hits the slug format URL (<code>/ping/key/slug</code>) using that project's key, HealthyCron can automatically provision a new monitor inside that target Project.
    </div>
</div>
